Hmm wait — lock ordering: settle locks withdrawal row first (lockByKey), then reservation rows, then ledger, then item rows. Receipt locks reservation row, then ledger, then item row, then updates withdrawal (completeIfAllTerminal is a conditional UPDATE — takes row lock on withdrawal). So receipt: reservation → ledger → item → withdrawal. Settle: withdrawal → reservation → ledger → item. Cycle: settle holds withdrawal lock, wants reservation lock; receipt holds reservation lock, wants withdrawal lock (at completeIfAllTerminal). Deadlock possible!

